---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import { links } from '../content/links';
import { featuredPublication, previousPublications, publicationDownloads } from '../content/publications';

const questions = ['What survives?', 'What transforms?', 'What must be reinvented?'];
const workstreams = [
  'Leadership development',
  'Talent management',
  'Performance & reward',
  'Workforce management',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Horizon Collective | Shaping the future of work"
  description="A 2–3 year movement exploring how work and organisations may evolve in the age of AI, led by thinkers and practitioners."
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <nav id="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href={links.sections.movement}>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--full">The movement</span>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--short">Movement</span>
      </a>
      <a href={links.sections.publications}>Publications</a>
      <a href={links.sections.team}>Team</a>
      <a href={links.sections.workstreams}>Workstreams</a>
      <a class="button button--small" href={links.contact.joinCollective}>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--full">Join the collective <ArrowIcon /></span>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--short">Join <ArrowIcon /></span>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-lockup" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg class="hero-horiz" viewBox="0 0 271.7 58.9" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-word"></use></svg>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <svg class="hero-zon" viewBox="228.9 0 168.8 58.9" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-word"></use></svg>
          <svg class="hero-collective" viewBox="175 77 224 29" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-collective"></use></svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 class="sr-only" id="hero-title">Horizon Collective — a movement for the future of work</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section intro" id="movement" aria-labelledby="movement-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The movement</p>
        <h2 id="movement-title">The world of work<br />is being rewritten.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p class="lead">The Horizon Collective is a 2–3 year <strong>movement</strong> where we are constantly evolving our thinking and understanding of the world of work and organisations in 7–10 years out.</p>
        <p>Through a combination of crowdsourcing from <strong>thinkers</strong> and testing these with <strong>practitioners</strong>, we develop a point of view and provide guidance about the transformation changes in the world of work, as a result of AI.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--lime">The questions</p>
        <h2 id="questions-title">The questions are<br />bigger than the <br class="answers-break" /><em>answers.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>At this point in time, we are not sure exactly how the classic HR fields are going to play out. We also don’t have a view yet how L&D, Reward and some other areas are going to shape up.</p>
        <p>We also do not know yet if the employee lifecycle as a concept will survive. Maybe we need to completely reimagine and evolve all these HR areas—and understand why the speed and depth of implementation differs across companies and industries.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-list" aria-label="Questions we are exploring">
        {questions.map((question) => <li>{question}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>

    <section class="section manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who is it for</p>
        <h2 id="manifesto-title">“A duty of care <br />for the future.”</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>The target group for the Horizon Collective are senior HR leaders and executives in roles where they are expected to have a point of view and who feel a <strong>duty of care for the future.</strong> And who also feel the urgency and have the agency to drive this forward.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>

    <section class="section work" aria-labelledby="work-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2 id="work-title">Distinct<br />workstreams.<br />One collective<br />horizon.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>We will establish several workstreams: leadership development, talent management, performance and reward, workforce management, and more.</p>
        <p>Each workstream will have a <strong>curator</strong>; someone who will guide and facilitate the development of a point of view about a specific area. We will also invite senior academics, consultants and thought leaders to act as our <strong>council of wisdom</strong>.</p>
        <ol class="stream-list">
          {workstreams.map((stream, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{stream}</li>)}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section workstreams" id="workstreams" aria-labelledby="workstreams-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div class="workstreams-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The workstreams</p>
          <h2 id="workstreams-title">Ideas into<br /><em>action.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p class="workstreams-deck">Focused explorations into the choices that will shape work and organisations over the next seven to ten years.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workstream-cards">
        <article class="workstream-card">
          <h3>Organisation Design & AI-Native Operating Models</h3>
          <p>You cannot drop AI into an Industrial-era operating model and expect the organisation to change. Our Zürich session brought the challenges into focus: AI ownership sits with whoever holds the tokens. Agents are mushrooming and nobody is pruning. Abundant intelligence has not become collective intelligence; coordination is becoming the scarcest resource in the enterprise.</p>
          <p>What could organisations become over the next seven to ten years, as AI becomes woven into how work happens? And what must we begin changing today to shape that future consciously?</p>
          <p>This workstream explores how organisations can evolve into living systems where humans and AI both flourish. Building on the Collective’s New Workforce Ecosystem, we will draw on the five pillars of the AI-Enabled Living System: distributed authority, fluid structure, evolutionary purpose, human wholeness and human–agent governance. Where might authority and accountability sit? How will work flow across organisational boundaries? How should humans and agents make decisions together? What will sustain judgement, creativity, trust and belonging?</p>
          <p>Through shared inquiry, participants’ experience and practical experiments, we will work backwards from the futures we want to create, identifying design principles, transition choices and experiments we can begin today. Our findings will connect with the futures and leadership workstreams and contribute to the Collective’s playbook.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="workstream-card">
          <h3>Four Futures of Work: different paths to Horizon 3</h3>
          <p class="workstream-question">“Why might AI transform work at different speeds and in different ways across industries, and how can leaders shape the outcomes?”</p>
          <p>Alongside the Collective’s white paper, we will use the Four Futures of Work framework I developed as a starting point for our shared exploration. Through four contrasting scenarios, we will consider how AI capabilities, adoption and leadership choices could shape work over the next seven to ten years. We will examine what accelerates or limits change across industries, and how deeply AI changes tasks, roles and business models.</p>
          <p>We will also explore what organisations do with the capacity it creates: improve services, develop new sources of growth, invest in people, reduce costs, or combine these choices. Practitioners’ experiences will be central to this work. Alongside research, we will bring together company examples, compare different contexts and test our assumptions. The aim is to develop shared insights and practical questions that help leaders recognise emerging changes and consider what they should begin preparing for today.</p>
          <p>This exploration will connect closely with the leadership and organisation design workstreams.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section publication" id="publications" aria-labelledby="publication-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <figure>
        <a class="publication-cover-link" href={featuredPublication.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Open ${featuredPublication.title} in a new tab`}>
          <img src={featuredPublication.cover.src} width={featuredPublication.cover.width} height={featuredPublication.cover.height} alt={featuredPublication.cover.alt} loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--lime">Publications</p>
        <h2 id="publication-title">A foundation <br />made to evolve.</h2>
        <p>This publication is the first step in a 2-3 year movement where we will explore with thinkers and practitioners how this new world of work is going to play out in many areas of HR. This journey is not an extrapolation of <strong>today+AI</strong>, but rather a complete re-imagination of work, HR and organizations in a future perspective. It will force us to <strong>dream the future</strong> and start developing concepts that are going to work in the years to come, when AI will diffuse with an accelerated pace. The future is not a foregone conclusion and the Horizon Collective aims to help us build this future.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          {publicationDownloads.map((publication) => (
            <a
              class:list={['button', publication.style === 'light' && 'button--light']}
              href={publication.url}
              download={publication.downloadName}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              <span class="button-label">{publication.buttonLabel}</span>
              <ArrowIcon direction="down" />
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section involvement" aria-labelledby="involvement-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Choose your level of involvement</p>
        <h2 id="involvement-title">Read.<br />Contribute.<br /><em>Shape.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="involvement-copy">
        <div class="involvement-content">
          <span class="squiggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="body-copy">
            <p>You can decide yourself how involved you want to be. Being <strong>just a</strong> curious reader is fine, contributing to a particular workstream is fine, or anything in between. Most importantly: you should feel free and comfortable with the choices you make.</p>
            <p>We will make sure to share with you what we are working on, who the curators will be and how you can contribute. You will also ensure it all gets tied up in the collective and that we keep posting regularly about developments inside the Horizon Collective.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button involvement-cta" href={links.contact.joinCollective}><span class="button-label">Join the collective</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="aside">Curious reader or active contributor — <em>there is no wrong way to take part.</em></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section initiators" id="initiators" aria-labelledby="initiators-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div class="initiators-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The initiators</p>
          <h2 id="initiators-title">Two perspectives.<br />One shared inquiry.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The Horizon Collective is a joint initiative from Ruud Rikhof at <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>brooksmiller</strong></a>, together with a group of workstream leads exploring how work and organisations are evolving.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="people-grid">
        <article>
          <img src="/ruud.jpg" width="721" height="692" alt="Portrait of Ruud Rikhof" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>Ruud Rikhof</h3>
          <p class="role">Founder · Transforming HR leadership · Research · Executive search</p>
          <p>The career of <a href={links.people.ruudLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ruud Rikhof</a> is a blend of international HR leadership experience, research-based insight, and executive search in the Human Resources domain.
The HR career was shaped, amongst others, at IBM, Bristol-Myers Squibb, Novartis, and UBS, working globally and based out of the Netherlands, Austria, the UK, Germany, and Switzerland. In local, regional, and global positions. He was the co-founder of KennedyFitch, a recognised brand for executive search, people advisory and leadership & transformation. In parallel, he has been active in building and connecting HR communities, including as co-founder of the Beyond HR Forum.
A consistent thread in his work is research and thought leadership and he has (co-)authored several studies on the evolving role of HR and the new world of work, which continues to inform his perspective and practice. At Brooksmiller, he focuses on executive search in the HR domain. </p>
          <div class="person-links" aria-label="Ruud Rikhof links">
            <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">brooksmiller <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={links.people.ruudLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Ruud Rikhof on LinkedIn">LinkedIn <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={`mailto:${links.contact.ruudEmail}`}>{links.contact.ruudEmail}</a>
          </div>
          <div class="previous-publications">
            <p>Previous publications</p>
            <ul>
              {previousPublications.map((publication) => (
                <li><a href={publication.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>{publication.title}</span><ArrowIcon /></a></li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <img src="/breeze-dong.jpg" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Chunfeng Breeze Dong" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>Breeze Dong</h3>
          <p class="role">Workstream Lead · Organisation Design & AI-Native Operating Models</p>
          <p><strong>Breeze Dong</strong> is an organisation designer, executive coach and author exploring how organisations and people can flourish in the AI era. She currently works in Organisational Development at Roche, focusing on operating model effectiveness. Her experience spans more than 20 years across Roche, ABB, Siemens and Roland Berger. Founder of <a href={links.organizations.springbreezeVentures} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Springbreeze Ventures</a>, Breeze combines an engineering background and an MPhil from Cambridge with psychology, ICF PCC executive coaching and mindfulness practice. She is co-author of <a href={links.organizations.livingOrganization} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Living Organization</a> and architect of its AI-Enabled Living System framework. Her work centres on a consequential choice: we are deciding, in a narrow window, what work will feel like for a generation. She helps leaders make that choice consciously, evolving organisations from machines that manage people into living systems where humans and AI both flourish.</p>
          <div class="person-links" aria-label="Chunfeng Breeze Dong links">
            <a href={links.organizations.springbreezeVentures} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Springbreeze Ventures <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={links.organizations.livingOrganization} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Living Organization <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={links.people.breezeLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn <ArrowIcon /></a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <img src="/juraj-ondrejkovic.png" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Juraj Ondrejkovic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>Juraj Ondrejkovic</h3>
          <p class="role">Workstream Lead · Four Futures of Work: different paths to Horizon 3</p>
          <p><strong>Juraj Ondrejkovic</strong> brings more than 20 years of experience in HR, talent and organisational change across the World Economic Forum, Syngenta, Thermo Fisher Scientific and The Adecco Group. His work has included developing leaders, building talent systems, leading HR for global businesses and reshaping operating models. At the World Economic Forum, he helped build the Global Leadership Fellows Programme, connecting leadership development with the challenges of working across sectors and cultures. The programme later became the subject of a Harvard Business School case study. He currently advises on organisation design and responsible AI adoption, including AI in recruitment. He enjoys exploring new possibilities with others, testing ideas in practice and turning shared insights into better ways of working.</p>
          <div class="person-links" aria-label="Juraj Ondrejkovic links">
            <a href={links.people.jurajLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn <ArrowIcon /></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <h2 id="closing-title">The future of<br />work will not<br />shape <em>itself.</em></h2>
      <div>
        <p>Join us and help shape the future through ideas, research, workshops and action.</p>
        <a class="button" href={links.contact.joinCollective}><span class="button-label">Join the conversation</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer data-nav-theme="dark">
    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>
    <div class="footer-inner" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <p>Powered by <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">brooksmiller</a></p>
      <p>© 2026 Horizon Collective</p>
      <p>Website by <a href={links.credits.monire} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moniré</a></p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const revealItems = Array.from(
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('main section:not(.hero) > *')
    );
    const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    revealItems.forEach((item, index) => {
      item.dataset.reveal = '';
      item.style.setProperty('--reveal-delay', `${(index % 3) * 90}ms`);
    });

    if (reducedMotion || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
      revealItems.forEach((item) => item.classList.add('is-visible'));
    } else {
      const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
          entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        });
      }, {
        threshold: 0.08,
        rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px',
      });

      revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
